<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>pokéharness</title>
<meta name="description" content="pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden. watch it work instead of staring at a terminal.">
<meta property="og:title" content="pokéharness">
<meta property="og:description" content="pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden. watch it work instead of staring at a terminal.">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://pokeharness.parthkohale.com/og.png">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Press Start 2P';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/press-start-2p-latin-400.woff2') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/inter-latin-var.woff2') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('/fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin-var.woff2') format('woff2');
  }

  :root {
    --ground-0: #17171B;
    --ground-100: #1D1D22;
    --ground-200: #26262C;
    --border: #787684;
    --ink-900: #DEDBD6;
    --ink-700: #B3B0AC;
    --ink-500: #96919F;
    --gold: #E8B740;
    --on-accent: #1A1320;
    --coral: #E08C82;
    --mint: #74C096;
    --sky: #6FB3C4;
    --lemon: #CFAA57;
    --lilac: #A896E3;
    --peach: #DFA57F;
    --font-display: 'Press Start 2P', monospace;
    --font-ui: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html { color-scheme: dark; }

  /* The page used to sit on one flat --ground-0 slab top to bottom. This
     layers two things over it instead: a fine 4px grain (axis-aligned so it
     stays crisp, no diagonal antialiasing) for a CRT/GB-screen texture, and
     a tall gradient that cycles gently through the three ground tokens
     down the whole document — background-size 100% 100% sizes it against
     the html element's box (the CSS root-background propagation rule hands
     body's background to the canvas when html itself paints none), which
     is identical to body's own box today since html has no explicit
     height, but isn't guaranteed to stay that way. Section-to-section
     rhythm on top of this base layer comes from the full-bleed .band-*
     wrappers further down, not from this gradient's own (deliberately
     gentle) steps. background-attachment stays at its "scroll" default
     throughout (never "fixed") to avoid the repaint jank fixed backgrounds
     cause on mobile Safari. */
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background-color: var(--ground-0);
    background-image:
      repeating-conic-gradient(rgba(232, 183, 64, 0.03) 0 25%, transparent 0 50%),
      linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        var(--ground-0) 0%,
        var(--ground-100) 10%,
        var(--ground-0) 24%,
        var(--ground-200) 40%,
        var(--ground-0) 58%,
        var(--ground-100) 76%,
        var(--ground-0) 92%,
        var(--ground-0) 100%
      );
    background-repeat: repeat, no-repeat;
    background-size: 4px 4px, 100% 100%;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  a { color: var(--gold); }

  img { display: block; max-width: 100%; }

  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  /* ── top wordmark ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .brand-row {
    /* padding-block (not the "padding" shorthand) so it layers on top of
       .wrap's own padding-inline instead of zeroing it out — every section
       below that only needs to override vertical spacing follows the same
       pattern, to keep .wrap's 24px side gutters intact at every width. */
    padding-block: 24px 0;
  }
  .brand {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* ── hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 40px;
    padding-block: 56px 44px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero-text {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .hero p.subhead {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* Decorative pixel-framed panel filling the empty right half of the hero
     at wide viewports. aria-hidden in the markup below since it's flavor,
     not content — the actual copy lives in .hero-text. */
  .hero-panel {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 300px;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .hero-panel-frame {
    position: relative;
    padding: 22px 20px 20px;
    background:
      repeating-conic-gradient(rgba(232, 183, 64, 0.05) 0 25%, transparent 0 50%) 0 0 / 4px 4px,
      var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.35),
      inset 2px 2px 0 0 rgba(222, 219, 214, 0.05),
      inset -2px -2px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    clip-path: polygon(
      0 10px, 10px 10px, 10px 0,
      calc(100% - 10px) 0, calc(100% - 10px) 10px, 100% 10px,
      100% calc(100% - 10px), calc(100% - 10px) calc(100% - 10px), calc(100% - 10px) 100%,
      10px 100%, 10px calc(100% - 10px), 0 calc(100% - 10px)
    );
  }
  .hero-panel-label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 8px;
    line-height: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .hero-panel-label::before {
    content: '> ';
  }
  .hero-panel-line {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .hero-panel-status {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .hero-panel-status p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-500);
  }
  .hero-panel-status p::after {
    content: attr(data-value);
    color: var(--value-color, var(--ink-900));
  }
  /* Stepped pixel corners (NES/GB dialog-box style), reused at a few sizes
     below via the --cut custom property: cuts an 8-bit "stair" out of each
     corner instead of the smooth curve border-radius would give — this
     design system has no rounded corners anywhere, so this is the pixel-art
     substitute for chrome that would otherwise reach for border-radius. */
  .btn,
  .tag {
    --cut: 6px;
    clip-path: polygon(
      0 var(--cut), var(--cut) var(--cut), var(--cut) 0,
      calc(100% - var(--cut)) 0, calc(100% - var(--cut)) var(--cut), 100% var(--cut),
      100% calc(100% - var(--cut)), calc(100% - var(--cut)) calc(100% - var(--cut)), calc(100% - var(--cut)) 100%,
      var(--cut) 100%, var(--cut) calc(100% - var(--cut)), 0 calc(100% - var(--cut))
    );
  }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 12px 22px;
    border-radius: 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: opacity 120ms ease, box-shadow 120ms ease, transform 80ms ease;
  }
  .btn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: default;
  }
  /* The global :focus-visible rule's outline-offset:2px puts the ring
     outside the stepped clip-path above, so it gets clipped away entirely
     on every .btn — pull it back inside the shape instead. */
  .btn:focus-visible {
    outline-offset: -6px;
  }
  .btn-primary:focus-visible {
    outline-color: var(--on-accent);
  }
  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--on-accent);
    box-shadow:
      inset 3px 3px 0 0 rgba(255, 246, 214, 0.45),
      inset -3px -3px 0 0 rgba(26, 19, 32, 0.4);
  }
  .btn-primary:hover:not(:disabled) {
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .btn-primary:active:not(:disabled) {
    transform: translateY(2px);
    box-shadow:
      inset -3px -3px 0 0 rgba(255, 246, 214, 0.3),
      inset 3px 3px 0 0 rgba(26, 19, 32, 0.4);
  }
  .btn-secondary {
    background: var(--ground-200);
    color: var(--ink-900);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.5),
      inset 2px 2px 0 0 rgba(222, 219, 214, 0.08),
      inset -2px -2px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover:not(:disabled) {
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px var(--gold),
      inset 2px 2px 0 0 rgba(222, 219, 214, 0.08),
      inset -2px -2px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .btn-secondary:active:not(:disabled) {
    transform: translateY(2px);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.5),
      inset -2px -2px 0 0 rgba(222, 219, 214, 0.08),
      inset 2px 2px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .eyebrow::before {
    content: '> ';
  }

  /* ── demo frame ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .demo-shell {
    padding: 8px 0 8px;
  }
  .window-chrome {
    background: var(--ground-200);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    padding: 8px 10px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 7px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .dot {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .dot-red { background: #FF5F57; }
  .dot-yellow { background: #FEBC2E; }
  .dot-green { background: #28C840; }
  .demo-frame-body {
    background: var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    border-top: none;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
  }
  /* The demo has its own internal breakpoints tuned for a real desktop app
     window and breaks down below ~1100px of *iframe* width (the party
     rail's collapse to a 56px face-tile column, and the topbar usage chip's
     own collapse, both fire at exactly max-width: 1100px — index.css). 1040
     used to sit just under that, so the embed always showed the collapsed
     rail. Rather than let the iframe shrink (which would trigger those
     internal breakpoints and clip content), we render it at a fixed design
     width above 1100px and scale the whole box down visually with a
     transform — the iframe always sees 1200px of internal viewport, and the
     visitor sees it fit whatever space is available. 1200/750 keeps the
     same 16:10 ratio as the frame itself, so the scale factor is just
     container-width / 1200. */
  .demo-frame-scaler {
    width: 1200px;
    height: 750px;
    transform-origin: top left;
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
  }
  .demo-frame-scaler iframe {
    width: 1200px;
    height: 750px;
    border: 0;
    display: block;
  }
  /* .demo-shell (frozen) sets padding-block only, on purpose — its own
     frame chrome bleeds edge to edge. These are its non-frame children, so
     they get the standard 24px side gutter back explicitly. */
  .demo-shell > .eyebrow,
  .demo-intro,
  .demo-below {
    padding-inline: 24px;
  }
  .demo-intro {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .demo-below {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .demo-tour-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .demo-tour-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-500);
  }
  .demo-playall {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .demo-tour-grid,
  .demo-more-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr));
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .demo-caption {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    max-width: 720px;
    min-height: calc(1.5em * 2);
  }
  .demo-more {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .demo-more summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 8px 0;
  }
  .demo-more summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .demo-more summary::before {
    content: '▸ ';
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .demo-more[open] summary::before {
    content: '▾ ';
  }
  .demo-mobile-note {
    display: none;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .demo-mobile-note { display: block; }
  }
  /* .demo-caption's min-height tiers below are measured against the
     longest scene caption (currently the mega-evolution one, ~132
     characters) so the reserved space never shifts when captions change
     but also never sits empty: it wraps to 2 lines from 719px down to
     ~490px, and 3 lines from ~480px down through phone widths (24px side
     gutters already subtracted). Re-measure headless if a caption grows
     past ~132 characters. */
  @media (max-width: 719px) {
    .demo-caption { min-height: calc(1.5em * 2); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .demo-caption { min-height: calc(1.5em * 3); }
  }

  /* ── works with ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* The section washes below (.band-works, .band-how, .band-features,
     .band-footer) live on a plain unconstrained div wrapping each
     .wrap-bearing section, not on the .wrap element itself — .wrap caps
     out at 1100px, so a background painted directly on it would hard-stop
     in a vertical seam past that width instead of bleeding to the page
     edges. The band div has no max-width, so its background naturally
     covers the full viewport; deliberately not the calc(50% - 50vw) trick,
     since 50vw includes the scrollbar gutter on Windows and would add a
     horizontal scrollbar. */
  .band-works {
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 900px 260px at 30% 0%, rgba(232, 183, 64, 0.09), transparent 70%);
  }
  .works-with {
    padding-block: 40px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
  }
  .works-with-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .works-with-note {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--ink-500);
  }
  .tag {
    --cut: 4px;
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    background: var(--ground-200);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.3),
      inset 1px 1px 0 0 rgba(222, 219, 214, 0.06),
      inset -1px -1px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    padding: 5px 10px;
  }

  /* ── how it works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section {
    padding-block: 64px;
  }
  /* One band wrapper per .section (see .band-works above for why the
     background lives on the unconstrained wrapper, not .wrap itself) —
     a light warm wash behind "how it works", a cooler one behind "what's
     in the garden", so the page's overall background isn't the only thing
     carrying the section-to-section rhythm. */
  .band-how {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, rgba(38, 38, 44, 0.1));
  }
  .band-features {
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 1000px 400px at 70% 0%, rgba(111, 179, 196, 0.09), transparent 70%);
  }
  .section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .how-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 56px;
  }
  .how-step {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .how-media,
  .how-text {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .how-step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .how-text h3 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .how-text p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 440px;
  }
  .how-media img {
    width: 100%;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
  }
  .install-card {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 2.1;
    background: var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 26px 24px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
  }
  .install-line {
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .install-file {
    color: var(--ink-900);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ── feature grid ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .feature-card {
    background: var(--ground-100);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    border-left-width: 3px;
    border-left-style: solid;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .feature-media {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--ground-200);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .feature-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .feature-media.solid {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* These glyphs (★ ⚔ ☀ ☾) have emoji presentations that some platforms
       default to; the text stack here plus U+FE0E on each character (see
       markup below) keeps them flat monochrome shapes instead of color
       emoji. */
    font-family: var(--font-display), 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Sans Symbols 2', sans-serif;
    font-size: 26px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .feature-body {
    padding: 16px 18px 20px;
  }
  .feature-body h3 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--ink-900);
  }
  .feature-body p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── footer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Same band-wrapper reasoning as .band-works above — see that comment. */
  .band-footer {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1));
  }
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.2);
    padding-block: 32px 48px;
  }
  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .disclaimer {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  /* ── responsive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Hides above the existing 900px tier on purpose: the hero panel needs
     ~300px plus a 40px gap alongside .hero-text's 420px flex-basis, so it
     starts crowding out the hero copy before the layout's other tiers
     would otherwise kick in. */
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .hero-panel { display: none; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .how-step { flex-direction: column; }
    /* Step 2's media sits after its text in source order (for the
       media-right look at desktop widths), unlike steps 1 and 3 — pin
       media first for every step once stacked, so the rhythm reads the
       same way down the column regardless of each step's desktop side. */
    .how-media { order: 1; }
    .how-text { order: 2; }
    .features { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .features { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 30px; }
    .demo-tour-grid,
    .demo-more-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .demo-tour-grid,
    .demo-more-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

<!-- The tour/control buttons below are built at runtime from
     window.pokeDemo.scenes (see the script further down), so they never
     receive Astro's scoped data-astro-cid attribute and none of the rules
     above would ever match them. This block is deliberately global, but
     every selector is anchored under the static .demo-below class from the
     template so it can't leak beyond this one section. -->
<style is:global>
  .demo-below .tour-chip {
    /* The page's global `* { box-sizing: border-box }` is a scoped rule
       too, so it never reaches these runtime-created buttons — only a
       <button>'s UA stylesheet happens to make it border-box by default.
       Set it explicitly: width:100% plus padding plus border-left would
       otherwise overflow the grid track. */
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-900);
    background: var(--ground-200);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(120, 118, 132, 0.3);
    border: none;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    min-height: 48px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: box-shadow 120ms ease, filter 120ms ease, transform 80ms ease, border-color 120ms ease;
  }
  .demo-below .tour-chip:hover:not(:disabled),
  .demo-below .tour-chip:focus-visible {
    border-left-color: var(--gold);
    filter: brightness(1.18);
  }
  /* The page's scoped `:focus-visible { outline: ... }` rule doesn't reach
     these chips either, for the same reason — give them their own. */
  .demo-below .tour-chip:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--gold);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .demo-below .tour-chip:active:not(:disabled) {
    transform: translateY(1px);
  }
  .demo-below .tour-chip:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .demo-below .tour-chip.is-playing {
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--on-accent);
    border-left-color: var(--on-accent);
    filter: none;
  }
  .demo-below .demo-more-grid .tour-chip {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-700);
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    border-left-width: 2px;
  }
  .demo-below .demo-loading {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-500);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="wrap brand-row">
  <div class="brand">pokéharness</div>
</div>

<header class="hero wrap">
  <div class="hero-text">
    <h1>your coding agents, as pokémon in a garden</h1>
    <p class="subhead">pokéharness turns every claude, codex, or cursor session on your machine into a walker in a pixel-art garden. spawn one and watch it work instead of staring at a terminal.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness/releases/latest">download for mac</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/mavericksxx/pokemon-harness">browse the source</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-panel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="hero-panel-frame">
      <p class="hero-panel-label">session preview</p>
      <p class="hero-panel-line">a wild claude session appeared.</p>
      <div class="hero-panel-status">
        <p data-value="running" style="--value-color: var(--mint)">status: </p>
        <p data-value="edit" style="--value-color: var(--sky)">tool: </p>
        <p data-value="★ shiny" style="--value-color: var(--lemon)">badge: </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap demo-shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">live demo</p>
  <p class="demo-intro">try a scene below to see what it does.</p>
  <div class="window-chrome">
    <span class="dot dot-red"></span>
    <span class="dot dot-yellow"></span>
    <span class="dot dot-green"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="demo-frame-body" id="demo-frame-body">
    <div class="demo-frame-scaler" id="demo-frame-scaler">
      <iframe id="demo-iframe" src="/demo.html?embed=1" title="pokéharness live demo"></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="demo-below">
    <div class="demo-tour-head">
      <span class="demo-tour-label">pick a scene</span>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary demo-playall" id="demo-btn-showreel" disabled>loading…</button>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-tour-grid" id="demo-tour-grid">
      <p class="demo-loading">loading tour…</p>
    </div>
    <p class="demo-caption" id="demo-caption">loading the live demo. give it a second.</p>
    <details class="demo-more" id="demo-more">
      <summary id="demo-more-summary">more controls</summary>
      <div class="demo-more-grid" id="demo-more-grid">
        <p class="demo-loading">loading…</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <p class="demo-mobile-note">the garden view above is scaled down to fit small screens. the pixel detail and hover effects show up best on a bigger one.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function () {
    var DESIGN_WIDTH = 1200;
    var body = document.getElementById('demo-frame-body');
    var scaler = document.getElementById('demo-frame-scaler');
    if (!body || !scaler) return;
    function fit() {
      var scale = body.clientWidth / DESIGN_WIDTH;
      scaler.style.transform = 'scale(' + scale + ')';
    }
    fit();
    window.addEventListener('resize', fit);
  })();
</script>
<script>
  (function () {
    var iframe = document.getElementById('demo-iframe');
    var tourGrid = document.getElementById('demo-tour-grid');
    var moreGrid = document.getElementById('demo-more-grid');
    var moreSummary = document.getElementById('demo-more-summary');
    var caption = document.getElementById('demo-caption');
    var playAllBtn = document.getElementById('demo-btn-showreel');
    if (!iframe || !tourGrid || !moreGrid || !playAllBtn || !caption) return;

    // Every button on this page is built from window.pokeDemo.scenes (see
    // tools/demo/template.html's SCENES table) — never hand-listed here, so
    // the marketing page can't drift from what the demo actually exposes.
    var api = null;
    var chips = [];
    var chipsById = {};
    var tourScenes = [];
    var tourRunning = false;
    var tourCancelRequested = false;
    var pollFailed = false;

    function setCaption(text) {
      caption.textContent = text;
    }

    function sleep(ms) {
      return new Promise(function (resolve) { setTimeout(resolve, ms); });
    }

    // While the sequenced tour (below) is running, it owns chip.disabled
    // and playAllBtn entirely — the per-chapter pokedemo:busy events it
    // triggers (one per api.run() call) are ignored here so they can't
    // fight the tour's own start/stop state or flip playAllBtn back to
    // "play the full tour" mid-tour.
    function setBusyUI(isBusy) {
      if (tourRunning) return;
      chips.forEach(function (chip) {
        chip.disabled = isBusy;
        if (!isBusy) chip.classList.remove('is-playing');
      });
      playAllBtn.disabled = isBusy;
      if (!isBusy) playAllBtn.textContent = 'play the full tour';
    }

    function makeChip(scene) {
      var btn = document.createElement('button');
      btn.type = 'button';
      btn.className = 'tour-chip';
      btn.textContent = scene.label;
      btn.disabled = true;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (!api || api.busy || tourRunning) return;
        setCaption(scene.caption);
        chips.forEach(function (c) { c.classList.remove('is-playing'); });
        btn.classList.add('is-playing');
        api.run(scene.id);
      });
      chips.push(btn);
      chipsById[scene.id] = btn;
      return btn;
    }

    function render(scenes) {
      var tour = scenes.filter(function (s) { return s.group === 'tour'; }).sort(function (a, b) { return a.order - b.order; });
      var controls = scenes.filter(function (s) { return s.group === 'control'; }).sort(function (a, b) { return a.order - b.order; });
      tourScenes = tour;

      tourGrid.innerHTML = '';
      tour.forEach(function (scene) { tourGrid.appendChild(makeChip(scene)); });

      moreGrid.innerHTML = '';
      controls.forEach(function (scene) { moreGrid.appendChild(makeChip(scene)); });

      if (moreSummary) moreSummary.textContent = 'show every control (' + controls.length + ')';
      if (tour[0]) setCaption(tour[0].caption);
    }

    function enable() {
      chips.forEach(function (c) { c.disabled = false; });
      playAllBtn.disabled = false;
      playAllBtn.textContent = 'play the full tour';
    }

    // Sequences the tour from here instead of calling the iframe's own
    // showreel: each chapter goes through api.run()'s existing real-time
    // ceiling individually, so one hung scene can no longer wedge the
    // whole page the way an unbounded runShowreel() could. It also lets
    // this page — not the (hidden-in-embed) in-frame banner — highlight
    // the running chip and narrate every chapter, not just single clicks.
    async function runTour() {
      if (!api || !tourScenes.length) return;
      tourRunning = true;
      tourCancelRequested = false;
      chips.forEach(function (c) { c.disabled = true; });
      playAllBtn.disabled = false;
      playAllBtn.textContent = 'stop';
      for (var i = 0; i < tourScenes.length; i++) {
        if (tourCancelRequested) break;
        var scene = tourScenes[i];
        chips.forEach(function (c) { c.classList.remove('is-playing'); });
        var chip = chipsById[scene.id];
        if (chip) chip.classList.add('is-playing');
        setCaption(scene.caption);
        await api.run(scene.id);
        if (tourCancelRequested) break;
        await sleep(1200);
      }
      var wasCancelled = tourCancelRequested;
      tourRunning = false;
      chips.forEach(function (c) { c.classList.remove('is-playing'); c.disabled = false; });
      playAllBtn.disabled = false;
      playAllBtn.textContent = 'play the full tour';
      setCaption(wasCancelled ? 'stopped. click any scene to keep going.' : 'tour finished. click any scene to run it again.');
    }

    playAllBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (pollFailed) {
        retryPoll();
        return;
      }
      if (!api) return;
      if (tourRunning) {
        tourCancelRequested = true;
        setCaption('stopping the tour…');
        return;
      }
      runTour();
    });

    // Same-origin iframe (served from this site), so this is direct property
    // access on contentWindow, not postMessage. demo.html's own inline
    // script defines window.pokeDemo synchronously while it boots, but the
    // outer iframe's 'load' event can fire before that — poll briefly
    // instead of relying on 'load'.
    //
    // A slow connection can still be loading the demo well past a short
    // ceiling, so this doesn't give up after ~10s: it softens the message
    // at 5s but keeps polling, and only declares the demo unavailable after
    // 30s of nothing — at which point playAllBtn turns into a retry button
    // that reloads the iframe and starts the poll again, so a real failure
    // (404, thrown script) is still recoverable without a page reload.
    function startPoll() {
      var tries = 0;
      var poll = setInterval(function () {
        tries++;
        var found = iframe.contentWindow && iframe.contentWindow.pokeDemo;
        if (found) {
          clearInterval(poll);
          api = found;
          render(api.scenes);
          api.ready.then(enable);
          iframe.contentWindow.addEventListener('pokedemo:busy', function (e) {
            setBusyUI(e.detail.busy);
          });
        } else if (tries === 50) {
          setCaption('still loading the demo. this can take a moment on a slow connection.');
        } else if (tries > 300) {
          clearInterval(poll);
          pollFailed = true;
          tourGrid.innerHTML = '<p class="demo-loading">demo unavailable</p>';
          moreGrid.innerHTML = '<p class="demo-loading">demo unavailable</p>';
          playAllBtn.disabled = false;
          playAllBtn.textContent = 'retry';
          setCaption('the demo failed to load. click retry to try again.');
        }
      }, 100);
    }

    function retryPoll() {
      pollFailed = false;
      playAllBtn.disabled = true;
      playAllBtn.textContent = 'loading…';
      tourGrid.innerHTML = '<p class="demo-loading">loading tour…</p>';
      moreGrid.innerHTML = '<p class="demo-loading">loading…</p>';
      setCaption('loading the live demo. give it a second.');
      try { iframe.contentWindow.location.reload(); } catch (e) {}
      startPoll();
    }

    startPoll();
  })();
</script>

<div class="band-works">
  <div class="wrap works-with">
    <div class="works-with-row">
      <span>works with the coding-agent cli you already run</span>
      <span class="tag">claude</span>
      <span class="tag">codex</span>
      <span class="tag">cursor-agent</span>
    </div>
    <p class="works-with-note">free and open source. runs on your machine, no accounts, no cloud.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="band-how">
<section class="section wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">getting started</p>
  <h2>how it works</h2>
  <div class="how-steps">
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-media">
        <div class="install-card">
          <div class="install-line install-file">Pokéharness.zip</div>
          <div class="install-line">→ drag to /Applications</div>
          <div class="install-line">→ right-click, open, open</div>
          <div class="install-line">→ never asks again</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="how-text">
        <div class="how-step-num">1</div>
        <h3>download and open it</h3>
        <p>download the .zip and drag it to applications. gatekeeper asks for permission once: right-click, then open, then open again. it won't ask after that.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-text">
        <div class="how-step-num">2</div>
        <h3>spawn a session</h3>
        <p>point it at a project folder and pick a pokémon, or let it choose a random starter. it launches claude, codex, or cursor-agent the same way you would from a terminal.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/garden.png" alt="a few walkers roaming the garden, mid tool-call, with speech bubbles above them">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/battle.png" alt="two walkers squared up in a battle, move text floating overhead">
      </div>
      <div class="how-text">
        <div class="how-step-num">3</div>
        <h3>watch it work</h3>
        <p>tool calls show up as a speech bubble while the walker goes about its business in the garden. subagents spawn as battles. long sessions evolve.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band-features">
<section class="section wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">features</p>
  <h2>what's in the garden</h2>
  <div class="features">
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--coral)">
      <div class="feature-media solid" style="background: rgba(224, 140, 130, 0.14); color: var(--coral)">★︎</div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>shiny pokémon</h3>
        <p>every session rolls for shiny once, at 1-in-64 odds, and keeps it for life. a shiny session gets a sparkle burst and a star badge.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--mint)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/evolution.png" alt="an evolution ceremony mid-flash, the walker's old form as a white silhouette">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>evolution</h3>
        <p>working time adds up. cross a threshold and the walker plays an evolution ceremony: a flash, a silhouette, then the new form. some evolved forms fly instead of walk.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--sky)">
      <div class="feature-media solid" style="background: rgba(111, 179, 196, 0.14); color: var(--sky)">⚔︎</div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>subagent battles</h3>
        <p>a task tool call spawns a wild pokémon. when it's done, it walks up and fights the parent: lunges, hit flashes, move text overhead. battles play out one at a time, so finishes queue up if a few land close together.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--lemon)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/mega.png" alt="a mega-evolved charizard mid-battle, gold ring and sparkle burst around it, a floating 'mega evolved!' text overhead">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>mega evolution</h3>
        <p>dozens of species mega-evolve for the length of a battle, with a full ring, vortex, and plume ceremony. they revert once the fight ends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--lilac)">
      <div class="feature-media">
        <img src="/screenshots/arceus.png" alt="the garden replaced by a starfield cosmos, arceus floating and cycling through its type-plate formes">
      </div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>arceus</h3>
        <p>summon a real claude session as arceus. it's a permanent, gold-framed orchestrator that can hand work to any other session in the garden.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card" style="border-left-color: var(--peach)">
      <div class="feature-media solid" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(111, 179, 196, 0.2), rgba(26, 19, 32, 0.5)); color: var(--peach)">☀︎ ☾︎</div>
      <div class="feature-body">
        <h3>day and night</h3>
        <p>the garden tracks your local clock. lamps come on at dusk, and the pond catches moonlight overnight. it fades back to day at sunrise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

